M157's patch 0034 said what a checked-in configure result is: a claim about
the machine that ran configure. ffmpeg's config.h is the second one this port
has met, and it opens with the same words fontconfig's did - "Automatically
generated by configure" - above a HAVE_ for every link test that machine ran.

HAVE_GETAUXVAL is glibc's getauxval(3). What it gates on this architecture is
one #include of <sys/auxv.h> in libavutil/cpu.c; the call itself is reached
only from the ARM, PowerPC and RISC-V hardware-capability paths, none of which
is compiled for x86-64. So the whole cost of the wrong answer is a header that
is not there, and the whole of the fix is asking the compiler doing THIS build
instead of remembering an answer from another one.

__has_include is that question. It names no C library and no operating system,
and on every machine where the configure test passed it still gives 1.

diff --git a/third_party/ffmpeg/chromium/config/Chromium/linux/x64/config.h b/third_party/ffmpeg/chromium/config/Chromium/linux/x64/config.h
--- a/third_party/ffmpeg/chromium/config/Chromium/linux/x64/config.h
+++ b/third_party/ffmpeg/chromium/config/Chromium/linux/x64/config.h
@@ -328,7 +328,26 @@
 #define HAVE_ELF_AUX_INFO 0
 #define HAVE_FCNTL 1
 #define HAVE_GETADDRINFO 0
-#define HAVE_GETAUXVAL 1
+/* getauxval(3) is glibc's, and its presence is a link test that was run on
+   the machine that generated this file rather than on the machine being
+   built for - the first line of this file says so ("Automatically generated
+   by configure"). The only thing HAVE_GETAUXVAL gates on this architecture
+   is the #include of <sys/auxv.h> in libavutil/cpu.c; the call itself is
+   reached from the ARM, PowerPC and RISC-V hardware capability paths, none
+   of which is compiled for x86-64.
+
+   __has_include is the question the configure test was standing in for, and
+   it asks it of the compiler doing this build instead of remembering an
+   answer from another one. It names no C library and no operating system. */
+#if defined(__has_include)
+#  if __has_include(<sys/auxv.h>)
+#    define HAVE_GETAUXVAL 1
+#  else
+#    define HAVE_GETAUXVAL 0
+#  endif
+#else
+#  define HAVE_GETAUXVAL 1
+#endif
 #define HAVE_GETENV 1
 #define HAVE_GETHRTIME 0
 #define HAVE_GETOPT 1
